# Per-machine settings for this checkout. Copy to `etc/amphora.local` (gitignored) and
# edit — the stack itself is path-independent, so most machines need none of this.
#
#     cp etc/amphora.local.example etc/amphora.local
#
# Sourced as shell by bin/amphoractl before its defaults, so every value here wins.
# NEVER put API keys or passwords in this file. Secrets live in podman's secret
# store: `./bin/amphoractl secrets set`.

# Where everything the stack produces lives, as opposed to the code and config in this
# checkout. Beneath it:
#
#     projects/   the agent's work, one folder per project   -> /projects
#     outbox/     files the agent sends                       -> /mounts/outbox
#     backups/    volume snapshots
#     logs/       the sweep's log, the deploy log
#     archive/    superseded agent output, kept by hand
#
# Defaults to the checkout itself, which keeps a fresh clone self-contained. A live
# install sets it, so the checkout holds nothing but what git tracks plus this file.
# Only projects/ and outbox/ are shared with the podman machine; the folder itself
# must not be, and must not be inside any git repository.
#AMPHORA_RUNTIME_DIR="$HOME/amphora-runtime"

# The podman machine Amphora runs in, and the connection amphoractl uses to reach it.
# The machine is Amphora's alone: podman on macOS runs one VM at a time, so general
# container work belongs on another engine (see README, Prerequisites). A rootful
# machine's connection is <machine>-root; override only if yours is named otherwise.
#AMPHORA_MACHINE=amphora
#AMPHORA_CONNECTION=amphora-root

# Where the agent's projects live, if not <runtime>/projects.
#AMPHORA_WORKSPACE="$HOME/Code"

# Where files the agent sends are put (the agent sees /mounts/outbox), if not
# <runtime>/outbox. Keep it outside the projects folder and inside a folder the podman
# machine shares.
#AMPHORA_OUTBOX="$HOME/Amphora-outbox"

# Ownership of files the agent writes. Defaults to your own `id -u` / `id -g`, which
# is right on any machine — set these only when that detection is wrong.
#AMPHORA_UID=501
#AMPHORA_GID=20

# Extra folders exposed to the agent live in etc/mounts, not here — that file is data
# rather than shell, so a folder list can never become a code path. Manage it with
# `amphoractl mount add|rm|ls`; see etc/mounts.example. Override its location only if
# you keep it somewhere else.
#AMPHORA_MOUNTS_FILE="$HOME/.config/amphora/mounts"

# Obsidian — one switch for the whole feature. Optional and off by default: leave
# AMPHORA_VAULT unset and nothing is mounted, no sweep runs, and the stack behaves
# exactly like a checkout that never heard of Obsidian. Comment it out again on a
# machine or VM that has no vault and everything turns off together — that is the
# only edit such a machine needs.
#
# Point it at the VAULT ROOT. The folder holding the board (<vault>/Kanban by
# default) is what crosses into the container, reaching the agent at
# /mounts/kanban so it can read and move cards from Signal.
#
# Only the board crosses. The sweep (tools/obsidian-kanban/) runs on the Mac and
# reads the vault in place, so the agent has no route to your notes.
#
# The board folder must be one the podman machine shares, or it binds as an empty
# directory with no error anywhere. `amphoractl shares` lists what the machine needs;
# `amphoractl up` refuses a folder outside it; `doctor` checks what dind can actually see.
#AMPHORA_VAULT="$HOME/Obsidian/MyVault"

# Override only if the board does not live in <vault>/Kanban. Inert without
# AMPHORA_VAULT, so it can never leave the feature half-on.
#AMPHORA_VAULT_KANBAN="$HOME/Obsidian/MyVault/Boards"
#AMPHORA_VAULT_BOARD="Board.md"

# Where the scheduled sweep writes its log. Defaults to <runtime>/logs. Only
# tools/obsidian-kanban uses it.
#AMPHORA_LOG_DIR="$HOME/Library/Logs/amphora"

# Address the dashboard (port 9119, the only published port) is bound to on the Mac.
#AMPHORA_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1

# The zone cron schedules are read in (an IANA name). Defaults to this Mac's own zone at
# the time hermes is created, so it follows the Mac when it travels; set it to pin one.
# Applied by `amphoractl config push`; existing jobs keep their next run time until their
# schedule is re-set (README, "Timezone").
#AMPHORA_TIMEZONE="America/New_York"

# Resources given to the Hermes container.
#AMPHORA_HERMES_MEMORY=4g
#AMPHORA_HERMES_CPUS=2

# SELinux MCS level the hermes container runs at. Pinned so that files Hermes writes
# stay readable across recreates; any s0:cN,cM with N < M <= 1023 will do. Changing it
# strands everything written under the old value until the volume is levelled — see
# `amphoractl doctor`.
#AMPHORA_HERMES_MCS_LEVEL=s0:c421,c907

# Image overrides. Hermes is pinned in lib/settings.sh; setting it here overrides that pin,
# later ones included, so prefer changing the pin.
#AMPHORA_HERMES_IMAGE=docker.io/nousresearch/hermes-agent@sha256:<digest>
#AMPHORA_SANDBOX_BASE=docker.io/nikolaik/python-nodejs:python3.11-nodejs20
#AMPHORA_DIND_IMAGE=docker.io/library/docker:dind
#AMPHORA_SEARXNG_IMAGE=docker.io/searxng/searxng:latest

# Volume snapshots. Defaults to <runtime>/backups, keeping the newest 14. Point the
# directory at an external disk if you want the snapshots off this machine's disk.
#AMPHORA_BACKUP_DIR="$HOME/Backups/amphora"
#AMPHORA_BACKUP_KEEP=14

# Paths inside a volume that are skipped as caches, taking a snapshot from ~1.8 GB to
# ~55 MB. Everything here is refetched by the agent on demand, which is why a restore
# needs network on first use. Drop ./bin from the list if you want a restore that can
# bootstrap offline. These apply to hermes-data only — amphora-signal-data is copied whole,
# because ./.local/share there is the Signal account's identity keys.
#AMPHORA_BACKUP_EXCLUDE="./home/.cache ./home/.npm ./.cache ./lazy-packages ./.local/share ./.cua-driver/packages ./bin ./skills/.hub/index-cache ./cache/web"

# Signal. Leave AMPHORA_SIGNAL_ACCOUNT unset and the Signal container, volume and network
# are never created — the stack behaves exactly as it does without Signal.
#
# The agent gets its own Signal account on a spare number; you message it as a contact.
# Enrol it with `amphoractl signal register` — see the Signal section of README.md.
#AMPHORA_SIGNAL_ACCOUNT="+15550100000"

# Who may talk to the agent, and whom it may write to. E.164 numbers, and ACI UUIDs where a number is not enough:
# Signal only includes the sender's number in sealed-sender messages, which need the
# profile key, so a first contact can arrive as a bare UUID and is matched literally.
# A refused sender prints its uuid in the hermes log — add it here.
#AMPHORA_SIGNAL_ALLOWED="+15550100000,7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7"

# Groups the agent answers in, by group ID; unset, group messages are ignored. Each group
# is a session of its own, with its own history and its own /model, so a group holding
# you and the bot is a second chat window. Senders are still matched against
# AMPHORA_SIGNAL_ALLOWED. Create the group in the app, then run `amphoractl signal groups`,
# which offers each group the bot is in, writes this line and offers the config push.
# "*" is refused.
#AMPHORA_SIGNAL_GROUPS="aBcD...=,eFgH...="

# Where cron jobs and proactive messages are delivered. Usually your own number; it must be
# on AMPHORA_SIGNAL_ALLOWED, or be group:<id> for a listed group.
#AMPHORA_SIGNAL_HOME="+15550100000"

# Swap to ...signal-cli-jre:latest if the native build misbehaves during registration.
#AMPHORA_SIGNAL_IMAGE=registry.gitlab.com/packaging/signal-cli/signal-cli-native:latest

# Email. Leave AMPHORA_EMAIL_ADDRESS unset and nothing email-related reaches Hermes. The
# agent gets a mailbox of its own — never a personal one, since IMAP credentials read the
# whole mailbox. The app password does NOT go here: `amphoractl secrets set email`.
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_ADDRESS="agent@example.com"

# The only addresses the agent corresponds with, both ways: the adapter ignores anyone
# else, and the mail relay refuses to send to anyone else.
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_ALLOWED="you@example.com"

# Where cron jobs and proactive messages are sent. Must be on the list above.
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_HOME="you@example.com"

# Required with the address. These are Google's; any IMAP/SMTP provider works. The SMTP
# host is only ever used by the relay — Hermes is pointed at the relay instead.
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_IMAP_HOST=imap.gmail.com
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com

# Trust only the provider's own Authentication-Results when deciding a sender is genuine.
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_AUTHSERV_ID=mx.google.com

# Optional; empty takes the defaults (993, 587 with STARTTLS or 465 for TLS, 15 seconds).
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_IMAP_PORT=993
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_SMTP_PORT=587
#AMPHORA_EMAIL_POLL_INTERVAL=15

# AI-watch feeds. Switched on by etc/feeds.csv (copy etc/feeds.csv.example), not by a
# variable here; these only tune it. FEEDS.md has the design.
# Where the fetcher writes batches for the agent. Must be a real folder, with no symlink
# on the way, inside a machine share. Default: <projects>/ai-watch/inbox.
#AMPHORA_FEEDS_INBOX="$HOME/amphora-runtime/projects/ai-watch/inbox"
# Seconds between fetches, at least 900. Default three hours.
#AMPHORA_FEEDS_INTERVAL=10800
#AMPHORA_FEEDS_IMAGE=amphora-feeds:local
